  "transfer": "Every identity common to the odd-prime finite division images holds over the integral right-zero extension, then on the reduction modulo two. The latter has a noninjective row, hence is not any left-division image. This rules out any set of defining identities. The same argument rules out a uniform term recovering source multiplication from division across this family.",
  "scopeCaution": "The uniform-term negatives concern reverse recovery from division, not the forward term-recovery fields in the parastrophe catalogue. Individual finite models still have reverse inverse terms.",
